<title>PERU: Peru sees $10 bln mining investment in decade.</title>
<headline>Peru sees $10 bln mining investment in decade.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1996-08-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peruvian Energy and Mines Minister Daniel Hokama predicted $10 billion of investment in Peru's mining sector over the next decade.</p>
<p>Hokama, quoted by government news agency Andina, said the privatization of state mining companies and the end to political instability had contributed to the boom Peru's mining sector is currently undergoing.</p>
<p>He added the only tax advantage which affect the sector was a clause in 1992 legislation governing mining investment that exempts companies from paying income tax on profits they reinvest.</p>
<p>-- Lima newsroom, 511 221-2134</p>
